{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q020_syntaxin_fragment_reclassification","answer":"SCOPe treats these fragments as incomplete examples of the syntaxin fold, not as evidence that syntaxin has a separate spectrin-repeat fold. In release 2.08, 1br0 (d1br0a_), all three classified chains of 1ez3 (d1ez3a_, d1ez3b_, d1ez3c_), and 1dn1 chain B (d1dn1b_) share the t-snare proteins family a.47.2.1, within the t-snare proteins superfamily a.47.2, STAT-like fold a.47, and All alpha proteins class a.

The annotations for d1br0a_ and d1ez3a_ explicitly describe three-helical fragments resembling one spectrin repeat and flag missing secondary structures comprising less than one-third of the common domain. The STAT-like fold is described as a four-long-helix bundle. Thus, the fuller structure supplies architectural context missing from the fragments: a locally convincing three-helix resemblance need not identify the complete domain's fold. Fragment-based assignments should be reconsidered when fuller structures become available; this is a correction of structural interpretation, not evidence of an evolutionary switch between folds.

Family and superfamily membership support an evolutionary relationship among these syntaxin structures. The shared STAT-like fold alone does not establish homology to STAT proteins or justify transferring STAT signaling functions; resemblance to spectrin likewise does not establish spectrin ancestry or function. The all-alpha class conveys only broad secondary-structure composition. Use fragments as templates only for their covered regions, not as complete-domain representatives. For present-day template selection, note that 1dn1 was superseded by 3c98; SCOPe's d1dn1b_ annotation identifies an automated match to d3c98b_. Check completeness, sequence correspondence, and coordinate quality before choosing a representative.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1br0/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1ez3/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47654/annotations"]}]}
